    "explanation": "Both parties: this dispute over the SGD 18.56 charged on trip TRP-00512 cannot be decided on the present record, so it goes to a human reviewer. Escalation is terminal: no money moves today, and the SGD 18.56 is held rather than collected or refunded.\n\nThe evidence. The GPS trace EV-GPS-00512 shows 8.92 km driven against a booked optimal of 6.1 km, an excess of 2.82 km (46.2%). But that trace is impaired: it contains a single 860-second gap between 19:23:30 and 19:37:50 and its coverage is only 44.9%. Its admissibility weight is 0.39 and its issue codes are GPS_GAP and LOW_COVERAGE. Under POL-RD-07(a) a gap above 90 seconds makes the trace impaired for policy purposes, so the deviation may not be established on the trace alone; POL-RD-07(ii) requires one of four independent corroborating sources, and none is present. The in-app chat EV-CHAT-00512 is empty (0 messages), so there is no driver admission in chat. The fare breakdown EV-FARE-00512 charges no ERP gantry that would place the vehicle on a corridor the optimal route does not use. trip_record.actual_distance_km of 8.9 km is a rounded convenience copy of the same trace measurement, which POL-RD-01 says may not be cited and which is not an independent derivation. That leaves the driver's own statement, and I have read it: it concedes a hung phone and an early end to the trip 600 m short of the rider's block, but it names no road, corridor or waypoint and says nothing about distance, so it is not 'a counterparty_statement admitting the route' within POL-RD-07(ii), and it would not support the deviation if the trace were removed.\n\nThe escalation trigger. POL-RD-07(iii) and POL-RD-10(3): the trace is impaired under POL-RD-07(a) to (c) and no corroborating artifact of the kind POL-RD-07(ii) names exists. POL-RD-10(1) reinforces this: the only weighted artifact carrying the deviation is EV-GPS-00512 at 0.39, below the 0.70 platform floor, and the counterparty statement carries no weight_multiplier, so it does not lift that cap under POL-GEN-02(2).\n\nWhat could not be used. To the rider: had the deviation been establishable, the POL-RD-02 arithmetic would give a recomputed fare of SGD 12.2550 ((3.80 + 0.75 x 6.1 + 0.28 x 11.0) x 1.0 surge, read from the fare breakdown, + 0.80 platform fee) and a refund of SGD 6.35 (18.56 - 12.2550 = 6.3050, rounded up to the nearest 0.05). That cannot issue while the trace is uncorroborated. Your remaining points stand: POL-RD-04 is unavailable (chat empty, no waypoint_hint), POL-RD-05 is unavailable (no endpoint amended, amended_optimal_distance_km null), POL-RD-11 and POL-RD-12 do not apply (RYDE_TAXI, METERED, quoted fare null), POL-RD-09 adds nothing (no gantry, toll, surcharge or waiting fee), and no POL-RD-06 repeat-deviation pattern is established (deviation_flags_90d 0 across 250 completed trips), so no conduct referral fires. To the driver: your hung-phone account is a device failure, and POL-RD-13 tests such an external-cause assertion against a traffic advisory and nothing else; no advisory is on file (EV-ADVIS-00512-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0), so it carries no weight under POL-RD-08. That does not win you the case, because POL-RD-07 and POL-RD-10(3) put the outcome on the trace, and the trace is impaired. The rider's account of navigation being switched off is likewise unsupported by any chat message.\n\nWhat would resolve it: a GPS trace with coverage across the 19:23:30-19:37:50 dropout; a chat-log admission from the driver; ERP gantry lines placing the vehicle off the optimal corridor; or a driver statement that actually admits the route driven. A human reviewer should obtain one of these. Referrals: none, because no clause produces one on these facts."
